The symbols identifiers resolved to, and the links of symbols, in pages of 64 ids

SparseLinkTable.get was 5.5 to 6.6% of the samples of every checker process of a garnet build,
nearly all at the read of the map's index (a table as large as everything stored, read where the
id's hash says) and the branch after it. getResolvedSymbol's lookup alone was 2.3% of a checker.

The ids of a file's nodes are consecutive, and so are those of the symbols a checker creates, so the
lookups of one function fall into a few pages of 64 ids (NearLinkTable). The symbols' links and the
resolved symbols of identifiers are stored for most ids of the pages they touch; the links of nodes
and the resolved types and signatures for few, and stay maps.

The checkers and forks of the TypeScript compiler project together, eleven alternating runs:
instructions 13.762 to 13.600 G (-1.2%), cycles 5.442 to 5.268 G (-3.2%), page faults +0.9%. With
all five tables in pages: instructions +0.7%, cycles -2.6%, page faults +4.4%.

